Relativity and gravitation (@relativity-and-gravitation: 0, is #chapter, #outline) { r_47N92WJBM5AJRF9NHTBBMT1JSW
Relativity studies spacetime, motion, causality, and gravitation beyond Newtonian descriptions. This material connects special and general relativity, curved geometry, gravitational waves, compact objects, and strong-field tests, explaining the observational and mathematical foundations and identifying unresolved questions about gravity.

**Common preparation developed:** the [spacetime and gravity common review](../core/Review-spacetime-gravity-and-orbital-evidence-before-astronomy.lingua) connects clocks, intervals, causal order, energy-momentum, inverse-square orbits, local equivalence, tidal structure and bounded weak-clock evidence. General tensor geometry, Einstein equations, strong fields, gravitational waves and advanced research remain in this pending scope.

**Parent:** [Physics — fields, matter, motion and physical evidence](../Physics.lingua#r_04A5CP8RTBERZEN4XCCDQ3T47W).
